    "node_index": 418,
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "While the U.S. Constitution requires only a population count every ten years via a decennial census, the ever-increasing need for more useful information about the United States' people, governments, businesses, and the economy drove the U.S. Census Bureau to evolve into the premier statistical agency of the federal government. Learn more about U.S. Census Bureau history and timeline, and the people, innovations and places that shaped it into what it is today.",
    "label": "unreviewed",
    "formatting": {}
  },
  {
    "node_index": 424,
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Agency History and Timeline In 1903, the Census Office was moved to the newly created Department of Commerce and Labor.",
